  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Schools Choose - Follow on for Kadama Caring Community Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the target community in Uganda, HIV/AIDS is stretching carers and severing generational ties on which societies depend for the transition of values and norms. Women and children are among the hardest hit. There is a constant risk of PLWHA and their children suffering neglect, abuse and deprivation that can be devastating. This application aoms to strengthen the ability of families of PLWHA to provide better and adequate protection, care and support to their children, and prevent the further spread of HIV. The project will provide psychosocial counselling, support to care givers, to children including financial, material, nutritional and family support delivered through home based care. Other activities will include training, mentoring volunteer carers, peer education with young people, outreach, home visits, income generating schemes and community partnership work for better child protection. The project will lead to more independent living for PLWHA, less dependence on children and better access to education for OVCs.</narrative>
  </description>
